#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:92
#: 726c1ffcd6af4462a45e34bf4fec419a
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:94
#: f9209e7292204652a84a38987333867d
msgid "The RX6 (UART6 RX), is by default is mapped to a timer input instead of the UART, and can be used for all ArduPilot supported receiver protocols, except CRSF/ELRS and SRXL2 which require a true UART connection. However, FPort, when connected in this manner, can provide RC without telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:96
#: 8e5e6eb343524524837a59ece3894c02
msgid "To allow CRSF and embedded telemetry available in Fport, CRSF, and SRXL2 receivers, the RX6 pin can also be configured to be used as true UART6 RX pin for use with bi-directional systems by setting the :ref:`BRD_ALT_CONFIG<BRD_ALT_CONFIG>` to “1” so it becomes the SERIAL6 port's RX input pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:98
#: 8852eab2e0a44d819e558873ff6f9b5e
msgid "With this option, :ref:`SERIAL6_PROTOCOL<SERIAL6_PROTOCOL>` must be set to \"23\", and:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:100
#: 5b7cd5c04a344e8695f27c4d1f8aa692
msgid "PPM is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:102
#: 8d104cb23532483c94f098d65e300013
msgid "SBUS/DSM/SRXL connects to the RX6  pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:104
#: d65777f5ed9745d0867fa3f89af06428
msgid "FPort requires connection to TX6 and RX6 via a bi-directional inverter. See :ref:`common-FPort-receivers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:106
#: 52fd37b106554dcd8ae24c86dc24f470
msgid "CRSF also requires a TX6 connection, in addition to RX6, and automatically provides telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:108
#: fd86f0b76afa46f0b670a1142a716ece
msgid "SRXL2 requires a connection to TX6 and automatically provides telemetry.  Set :ref:`SERIAL6_OPTIONS<SERIAL6_OPTIONS>` to \"4\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:110
#: 7dafeecfbd8e46c39d382b043a737cf1
msgid "Any UART can be used for RC system connections in ArduPilot also, and is compatible with all protocols except PPM. See :ref:`common-rc-systems` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:113
#: 37c7b456b7fe442992f8e5d9a1ffef67
msgid "USB Power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:115
#: 1502f44b91c94757b4ee041455fd46f6
msgid "When connected to USB, pins marked 5V are powered. Be careful not to overload the USB host's current capability. Powering the autopilot, and an RX and GPS is usually within most USB host's capabilities, however."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:119
#: 58b951d7c1cb4320863ea3b85e7f5a53
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:121
#: bee4d1f6524240408017c406bfa3da0a
msgid "The KakuteH7-Wing supports using its internal OSD using OSD_TYPE 1 (MAX7456 driver). External OSD support such as DJI or DisplayPort is supported using UART5 or any other free UART. See :ref:`common-msp-osd-overview-4.2` for more info."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:124
#: f327116d9ae44fe9ac732736991ee744
msgid "Camera and VTX Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:126
#: 5c221a97f569422f908be02833d01e13
msgid "The pin marked 9V (can be selected by jumper on the rear of the board to be 9V or 12V)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:128
#: 77d214bb71d54576ad2b27541ef86826
msgid "Switching between the two camera inputs, C1 (default on) or C2, and between on (default) and off of the 9V supply pin can be implemented using the Relay function of ArduPilot and assigning the relays to an ``RCx_OPTION`` switch on the transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:130
#: 2176c3dcf0324cd8a7ce46d13781d0fd
msgid "Set the ``RELAYx_PIN`` to \"82\" for on/off of 9V supply, and to \"81\" to control the camera switching. Then select an RC channel for control (Chx) and set its ``RCx_OPTION`` to the appropriate Relay (1-4) that you had set its pin parameter above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:133
#: 18ddc8f14a4048538441baf2b9571cf3
msgid "For example, use Channel 10 to control the camera switch using Relay 2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:135
#: 7dd60f7d19cc483a88811428d91ecae1
msgid ":ref:`RELAY2_PIN<RELAY2_PIN>` = \"81\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:136
#: 9d8fd1a285a34b66b41cb7d11df46504
msgid ":ref:`RC10_OPTION<RC10_OPTION>` = \"34\" (Relay2 Control)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:138
#: 9df7ad31e2894d1e9fd1e036c5bb272b
msgid "setting Relay on/high assigned for 9V pin will turn on that supply. Likewise, setting on/high for the Relay assigned for camera, will switch from Camera 1 to Camera 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:141
#: 493abd0344144da3ad8ed1178ce5214f
msgid "CAN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:143
#: f74b2c28a3cc4d6d9fcb868ed4f37279
msgid "The KakuteH7-Wing has one CAN port (port 1 parameters should be used) available for connecting CAN and DroneCAN peripherals such as GPS and airspeed sensors. See :ref:`common-canbus-setup-advanced` for more information on setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:147
#: db32ebcc4e084a059ed47f249b1e156d
msgid "Battery Monitor Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-kakuteh7wing.rst:148
#: 574202ca6258428c93ed3007b726d716
msgid "The board has a built-in voltage and current sensor. The current sensor can read up to 120 Amps. The voltage sensor can handle up to 6S LiPo batteries."
msgstr ""

